OL,4,CTitanic hero's postcard to sister      
OL,5,Csells for #32k                         
OL,6,GA postcard written by the Titanic's    
OL,7,Gsenior wireless operator has sold for  
OL,8,G#32,000 at auction, well over the      
OL,9,Gexpected price of up to #20,000.       
OL,11,FJack Phillips, 25, who came from       
OL,12,FSurrey, wrote the card to his sister   
OL,13,FElsie who lived in Godalming, while    
OL,14,Fthe ship was docked in Southampton on  
OL,15,F6 April 1912.                          
OL,17,FPhillips, who died in the disaster     
OL,18,Falongside about 1,500 others, remained 
OL,19,Fat his post sending wireless distress  
OL,20,Fcalls after the TItanic had struck an  
OL,21,Ficeberg.                               
OL,22,                                   G1/4 
