OL,4,CCampaigners say under-threat clock     
OL,5,Ccould be saved                         
OL,6,GCampaigners fighting to save a 73-year-
OL,7,Gold heritage floral clock in East      
OL,8,GSussex say it could be restored,       
OL,9,Gdespite the council saying it is       
OL,10,Gbeyond repair.                         
OL,12,FPlans by Brighton & Hove City Council  
OL,13,Fto remove the floral clock in Palmeira 
OL,14,FSquare, Hove, prompted opposition and  
OL,15,Fa petition signed by over 3,000 people.
OL,17,FFriends of Hove Floral Clock, which    
OL,18,Fhas applied to Historic England for    
OL,19,FGrade II listed status, want the       
OL,20,Fcouncil to pause replacement plans     
OL,21,Funtil that application has been        
OL,22,Fdetermined.                       G4/4 
